     1	"""One draw of the diagnostic same-day run (WIRING-DESIGN.md §A, §D; D447, D448; council mo, D449): a clean draw (Step 1 c8 → Steps 2–3
     2	→ the opened theses as cases → the ladder step → the frozen judge) or a production draw (v118 through `budget_replay`), every paid call on
     3	one shared ledger. One launcher process runs one draw; several draws run at once, each in its own folder `<root>/<label>`, on one ledger.
     4	
     5	**States** (`<root>/<label>/run.json`, written before and after each component): each attempt is `started`, `completed`, `stopped`
     6	(with its reason) or `crashed`. The draw is `running`, `complete`, `awaiting a redo decision` or `stopped`. The draw's kind, label,
     7	ledger and options are written at its first launch; a later launch that differs is refused.
     8	
     9	**The launcher is alive while it holds `<root>/<label>/launch.lock`.** Before it takes the lock it runs the ledger's dead-launcher check
    10	(under the ledger's lock, so its own new lock never hides a stale entry); after taking it, it registers the lock path on the ledger, and it
    11	removes the entry before releasing the lock on a normal end. A launcher that dies without removing it (a SIGKILL) is found by the stop
    12	gate before the next actual send of any process, which stops the ledger: its orphaned child's next send is refused, and so is every other
    13	draw's.
    14	
    15	**What stops the whole run** (the shared ledger's persisted stop): a budget refusal or an overrun; a crash (a component killed by a signal,
    16	a launcher interrupted, a launcher found dead, an attempt found `started`); a component that stops after its one redo, or that has no
    17	redo (the cases, the ladder step, the judge, whose own one redo is inside `run_stage_b`); a configuration that is not the frozen one.
    18	
    19	**The one redo** (Step 1, Step 2, production; D449): a first stop that is neither the ledger's nor a crash ends this draw only, as
    20	`awaiting a redo decision`. The redo is a later launch with `--redo <component> --redo-reason <text>`, made only when the component's
    21	output shows an eligible failure (a transport failure after its own retries, an answer refused or not fitting its schema); the reason is
    22	written to the record. Once per component, in a new folder; its stop stops the run.
    23	
    24	  python3 run_fresh.py clean --root R --label c1 --ledger L [--until-day 2026-07-01] [--passes 3] [--redo C --redo-reason TEXT]
    25	  python3 run_fresh.py prod  --root R --label p1 --ledger L [--until-day 2026-07-01] [--redo prod --redo-reason TEXT]
    26	
    27	A window other than the full run's (D486's lean step 2) is given with --manifest M: a Step 1 manifest whose items both systems read (built by
    28	`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/fresh_week_inputs.py`); the draw then runs from its from_day to --until-day (default its until_day).
    29	"""
    30	import argparse
    31	import ast
    32	import fcntl
    33	import hashlib
    34	import importlib.util
    35	import json
    36	import os
    37	import shutil
    38	import signal
