**The slice is not ready.** The 28 listed hashes match, and the astra wrapper computes the expected checksum. The remaining gaps affect what the run can prove and how its result can be scored. [Versions manifest](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/versions-manifest.json:2) · [Astra check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/run_fresh.py:53)

1. **Refuse the resequencing as proposed.** D665 freezes the controls, credit rules, versions and verdict before the first send. D667 also makes the review of built instruments a gate. The scorer, cards and reading procedure lack that proof. Pure reporting can move later under an explicit amendment, provided the run already captures what it needs. In particular, prove both July 14 states can be reconstructed or arrange snapshots before the full replay. [D665](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9423) · [D667](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9465) · [Freeze notes](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/freeze-review-notes.md:10)

2. **The verdict JSON is incomplete.** It gives 10 points and 10 cards without specifying that the limit is the *new* system’s share above the old system’s or that the minimum applies *per subgroup per system*. It also omits the moved rung, three plants per system, independent confirmation of supported controls, and hidden repeats. Freeze those details before sending. [Verdict JSON](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/verdict-rule.json:47) · [Plan §1.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v11.md:155)

3. **Prove the actual launch path.** The input proof stages the clean manifest from production’s routing calculation. It never launches either system and hashes only clean-side text. The judge test mocks the replay, so it proves argument forwarding rather than closing on a trailing day without articles. Run the required fake-answer dry runs through both real launchers. Compare their recorded IDs and text hashes, exercise an astra refusal and resend under the ledger, and prove the trailing-day close. The archive check also needs to require the expected checksum in **each** pass. Its current union lets an empty archive pass. [Input proof](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/comparison_inputs.py:25) · [Judge test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/test_ladder_adapter.py:502) · [Archive check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/run_fresh.py:396)

4. **Finish the pre-send checks.** The recorded preflight covers one historical v108 draw. The plan requires the latest stored answers from both systems. The size report covers production and its proxy, with no clean-side estimate recorded. The new launch wrapper checks listed hashes, but it can reuse an existing ledger without checking its ceiling. Freeze the wrapper and verify the actual slice ledgers and snapshot-based monitoring in the dry run. [Preflight output](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/preflight-output.txt:1) · [Run log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md:26) · [Launcher](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/launch_comparison.py:35)

NOT READY: freeze and prove the scoring instruments, complete the verdict rule, and pass the real-path dry runs and preflight.
